# Code-block step definitions — deliberate, visible black-box escapes.
#
#   ```js    evaluated IN-PAGE via agent-browser eval (last expression = result)
#   ```bash  evaluated LOCALLY from the project root (JSON on stdout = result)
#
# Result convention: JSON (or empty). The runner captures and reports it.
# Least-power ladder: prefer UI steps, then agent-browser natives
# (cookies/storage/set), then ```js in-page, then ```bash local.

step: the browser storage is empty
  ```js
  sessionStorage.clear();
  localStorage.clear();
  ({ cleared: true })
  ```

step: the api accepts order "{id}"
  ```bash
  curl -s -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/orders \
    -H 'content-type: application/json' \
    -d '{"id": "{id}", "status": "accepted"}'
  ```

step: the cart holds "{item}" for "{name}"
  ```js
  const key = 'cart:' + {name};
  const cart = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(key) || '[]');
  cart.push({item});
  localStorage.setItem(key, JSON.stringify(cart));
  ({ [key]: cart })
  ```
